# Tomato Ripeness Detection Using YOLOv8

A computer vision project for detecting tomato ripeness stages using the YOLOv8 object detection model.

## Project Overview

This project explores object detection for classifying tomatoes into three ripeness categories:

* **Green** — Unripe tomatoes
* **Half-Ripened** — Tomatoes transitioning toward ripeness
* **Ripened** — Mature tomatoes

The model is trained on an annotated tomato image dataset to identify and locate tomatoes in images.

## Technologies Used

* Python
* YOLOv8
* Computer Vision
* Object Detection

## Dataset

The repository contains tomato images for model training and experimentation. Refer to the dataset structure and annotations in the repository before running training or evaluation.

## Getting Started

1. Clone this repository.
2. Set up a Python environment.
3. Install the required dependencies for your YOLOv8 setup.
4. Configure the dataset paths and model settings.
5. Run the appropriate training or inference script.

## Future Improvements

* Evaluate detection performance on unseen images.
* Improve performance across lighting conditions and different backgrounds.
* Document evaluation metrics and example predictions.

